1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,760
I used OpenAI Codex to help build and

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:06,319
revise the app, check calculations and

3
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:09,360
primary sources, and draft documentation

4
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:12,240
and recording guides. The analysis and

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,639
decision are mine. This is an

6
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:16,800
educational project for a fictional

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,119
university scholarship fund, not

8
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:22,600
investment advice.

9
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:26,960
A user starts the app by running Python

10
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,439
run. py from this project folder. The

11
00:00:31,439 --> 00:00:33,600
launcher creates the environment,

12
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,480
installs the pinned dependency, and starts

13
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,920
Streamlit. First setup needs internet.

14
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:43,040
Afterward, calculations use bundled data

15
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:47,360
and no API key is required.

16
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:51,280
The interface is in app.py. It collects

17
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,920
the scenario controls, converts

18
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,800
percentage inputs into decimals, and

19
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,399
passes them to the model through

20
00:00:58,399 --> 00:01:00,000
settings.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,680
The solve function returns the

22
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,640
allocation and rule verdicts.

23
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,200
Invalid inputs or source problems

24
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,760
produce an error instead of a portfolio

25
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,760
recommendation.

26
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:14,320
The signal record function checks the

27
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:17,200
archived Federal Reserve evidence. It

28
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,840
verifies the rates units, publication

29
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:23,439
and effective dates and target bounds.

30
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:25,840
Further down, it checks both source

31
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:28,479
files against their recorded hashes and

32
00:01:28,479 --> 00:01:31,040
required supporting text.

33
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,119
Unsupported evidence stops the

34
00:01:33,119 --> 00:01:36,119
calculation.

35
00:01:40,079 --> 00:01:42,960
The estimates function caps SGOV's

36
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:45,360
historical annual mean at the policy

37
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:48,320
rates lower bound. This is a research

38
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:51,280
assumption, not an ETF yield or a

39
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:54,079
validated forecast.

40
00:01:54,079 --> 00:01:56,320
The evaluate function calculates each

41
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,799
portfolio's financial results. Net

42
00:01:58,799 --> 00:02:00,799
return equals weighted gross return

43
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:03,280
minus annual additional cost and trading

44
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:06,479
cost times turnover. Basis points are

45
00:02:06,479 --> 00:02:08,959
divided by 10,000.

46
00:02:08,959 --> 00:02:10,720
Turnover measures the change from the

47
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:13,040
paper reference weights, not verified

48
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,920
client holdings. Volatility uses

49
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:18,400
annualized covariance.

50
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,160
The measured rules check return,

51
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:23,040
reserve, turnover, and the proposed risk

52
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,640
ceiling.

53
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,640
Separate unresolved requirements keep

54
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,879
full mandate clearance at fail even when

55
00:02:28,879 --> 00:02:33,000
the numerical rules pass.

56
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:42,720
The allocations function generates all

57
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,239
1771

58
00:02:44,239 --> 00:02:46,720
combinations on a five percentage point

59
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:49,920
grid. The solver evaluates the baselines

60
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,000
and searches for the lowest volatility

61
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
candidate that passes every modeled

62
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,680
rule. If no candidate qualifies, it

63
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,640
returns a rejection. This establishes

64
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:03,519
infeasibility on this grid. It does not

65
00:03:03,519 --> 00:03:05,280
prove that every possible continuous

66
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:09,080
allocation would fail.

67
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,319
First, I'll change additional annual

68
00:03:12,319 --> 00:03:15,920
cost from 25 to 35.

69
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,920
Here is a direct check of the risk

70
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:20,959
constraint. At 35 basis points of annual

71
00:03:20,959 --> 00:03:24,319
cost and a 6% volatility ceiling, the

72
00:03:24,319 --> 00:03:27,920
current model selects 70% SGOV and

73
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:30,400
30% ACWI

74
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:34,799
with 4.54% volatility.

75
00:03:34,799 --> 00:03:37,680
Next, I'll change the proposed annual

76
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:42,519
volatility ceiling to 4%.

77
00:03:42,799 --> 00:03:45,440
Tightening the ceiling to 4% rejects the

78
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,959
scenario.

79
00:03:46,959 --> 00:03:49,280
No candidate on the grid satisfies the

80
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:51,519
return target together with the risk

81
00:03:51,519 --> 00:03:54,000
ceiling and other rules.

82
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,080
The model does not increase the risk

83
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:59,280
limit automatically.

84
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:04,319
Next, I'll restore the ceiling to 6%

85
00:04:04,319 --> 00:04:10,760
and restore annual cost to 25.

86
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,959
And you can see that restoring the

87
00:04:12,959 --> 00:04:15,280
original settings brings back the

88
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:19,120
baseline allocation and results.

89
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:22,160
The saved validation record reports 18

90
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,560
passing tests including source

91
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:28,240
tampering, future dates, risk boundary

92
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:31,600
behavior and app recovery. An additional

93
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:35,199
arithmetic audit reconciled 244 monthly

94
00:04:35,199 --> 00:04:38,880
prices and eight scenarios.

95
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,720
These are AI assisted development

96
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,600
checks. My original locked experiment

97
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,759
remains separately documented on its

98
00:04:45,759 --> 00:04:49,040
original model version. Together, the

99
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,800
evidence supports implementation

100
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,840
consistency, but it does not establish

101
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:56,720
forecast accuracy or suitability for

102
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:59,680
live investment.
